[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Several specification postconditions in this test module remain unverified: re-registration of an already-registered node identifier is never asserted, leaving the add_node postcondition that the supplied definition and its dependency edges become the registered ones uncovered; the critical-path postcondition for a graph containing no nodes is never asserted, leaving the empty longest-path sequence and its zero cumulative weight uncovered; scheduler synchronization is never asserted when a node enters tracking after its upstream dependencies have already succeeded, leaving promotion of newly available work to a runnable ready state uncovered; mark_succeeded is never asserted when a dependent has already reached a terminal state through an earlier upstream failure under the skip-downstream policy, leaving the requirement that promotion applies only to newly unblocked nodes uncovered; and skip-downstream transitive-dependent handling is never asserted when dependents are reachable through more than one dependency path, leaving the postcondition that each transitive dependent transitions to skipped uncovered.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: The implementation retains code that is unreachable under the contract closure: the defensive guard in the cycle-detection DFS for upstream identifiers absent from the graph can never fire, because every caller of cycle detection first verifies that all referenced dependencies exist and raises NodeNotFoundError before detection starts; the final pending-promotion pass in the CONTINUE_ON_ERROR branch of mark_failed re-applies the exact predicate already applied by the synchronization step invoked at the start of the same call, and the intervening pass only moves nodes to SKIPPED, so no pending node whose upstream dependencies have all succeeded can survive to be promoted there; and the empty-wave break in the run loop is a stall guard that cannot trigger during a run, since every dispatched node is resolved before the next iteration and the readiness predicate consulted by is_finished matches the one used to build the next wave. Restructure to eliminate this dead code, and annotate the defensive stall guard with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>)' per the unreachable-code methodology.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Resolve unreachable-code feedback: remove the redundant upstream-membership guard in DFS cycle detection (all callers pre-validate referenced dependencies), delete the no-op pending-promotion pass in the CONTINUE_ON_ERROR branch (synchronization already applies the same predicate and the intervening pass only marks SKIPPED), and annotate the defensive empty-wave stall guard with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: ...)'. Runtime re-verified across happy path, cycles, retries, all failure policies, removal purge, and empty DAG.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Added five postcondition tests addressing all feedback: (1) test_add_node_replaces_existing_registration asserts the newly supplied definition and its dependency edges replace a prior registration for the same node_id; (2) test_compute_critical_path_empty_graph asserts an empty graph yields an empty path list and zero cumulative weight; (3) test_state_sync_promotes_late_nodes_with_succeeded_upstreams asserts a node tracked after its upstream already succeeded is promoted to READY and returned by next_wave; (4) test_mark_succeeded_does_not_revive_terminal_dependents asserts a dependent already SKIPPED by an earlier skip-downstream failure is not promoted when another upstream succeeds; (5) test_mark_failed_skip_downstream_handles_multi_path_dependents asserts transitive dependents reachable through multiple dependency paths all transition to SKIPPED. Module now has 47 tests; static checks pass.
[AUDIT] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: QA_AUDIT
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: The re-registration coverage for the add_node postconditions leaves a graph-adjacency consistency aspect unasserted: when an identifier that was previously registered with declared upstream dependencies is registered again, no test verifies that the previously registered dependency edges are detached while the newly supplied dependency edges are established, so the invariant that a node's adjacency data corresponds to its currently registered definition is unverified; the existing re-registration scenario only exercises replacement when no earlier dependency edges existed, so the edge-removal aspect of re-registration and the dependency/dependent query postconditions after such a replacement remain uncovered.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Added test_add_node_reregistration_detaches_previous_dependency_edges to address the adjacency-consistency feedback: a node is first registered with declared upstream dependency previous_dep (asserting its dependency/dependent queries), then re-registered for the same node_id with a different upstream new_dep. The test asserts the previously registered edge is detached (get_dependents(previous_dep) is empty, get_dependencies(target) exactly {new_dep}), the newly supplied edge is established (get_dependents(new_dep) is {target}), and the derived graph queries (find_roots, find_leaves, validate, topological_sort) reflect only the currently registered definition's adjacency. Module now has 48 tests; static checks pass.
